BUANGKOK — third-party notices
==============================

src/pydoseia/ is a Rust port of parts of pyDOSEIA
(https://github.com/BiswajitSadhu/pyDOSEIA), commit
dca4cdc3bb0bef7f7e692c8991cf536c91e7a4ce, retrieved 2026-09-28. pyDOSEIA is
distributed under the MIT licence reproduced verbatim below. The ported files
carry this notice by reference and must keep it; the port as a whole is
distributed under GPL-3.0 (see the workspace LICENSE), which the MIT licence
permits.

No pyDOSEIA data file (library/, met_data/) is included in this crate.

src/pydoseia/quadpack.rs is a Rust port of SciPy's C translation of QUADPACK
(scipy/integrate/__quadpack.c, functions dqagse, dqk21, dqelg, dqpsrt; SciPy
tag v1.18.1, read 2026-09-28), because pyDOSEIA's plume-shine integral runs on
scipy.integrate.tplquad. That file is distributed under the BSD 3-clause
licence reproduced verbatim below. QUADPACK itself (R. Piessens,
E. de Doncker-Kapenga, C. Ueberhuber, D. Kahaner, 1983;
https://www.netlib.org/quadpack/) is in the public domain.

Associated paper (cited, not reproduced; (c) 2025 Health Physics Society):
B. Sadhu, T. Sarkar, S. Anand, K. D. Singh, D. K. Aswal, "pyDOSEIA: A Python
Package for Radiological Impact Assessment during Long-term or Accidental
Atmospheric Releases", Health Physics 130(1) (2026) 94-110,
doi:10.1097/HP.0000000000002014, PMID 40622262.

